From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/cix: reject audio startup on disconnected DP ports

Candidate fix for disconnected-port probing, NOT a claim of audible
audio repair. Hardware validation of this change is still pending.

On O6N, hw:0,0 is disconnected and opening it reproducibly emits
Unknown ELD version 0. Connected hw:0,1 has valid ELD, runs stereo
48 kHz playback, and emits no warning. Returning success when no
sink exists lets hdmi-codec continue into parsing the all-zero ELD
provided by get_eld. Return ENODEV before hdmi-codec reaches that
parse or marks the PCM busy. Preserve the connected startup path.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c
@@ -118,8 +118,9 @@
 	struct trilin_dp *dp = (struct trilin_dp *)data;
 	struct dptx_audio *dp_audio = &dp->dp_audio;
 
+	/* No sink: do not enable playback or parse an intentionally empty ELD. */
 	if (!trilin_dp_plugged_status(dp))
-		return 0;
+		return -ENODEV;
 
 	trilin_dp_write(dp, TRILIN_DPTX_SEC0_AUDIO_ENABLE, 1);
 
